 "notes": "Controller: state machine (pre -> descend -> close -> lift -> carry -> lower -> release -> retreat -> done) with retries. Hand pose is parametrized as palm-down with a yaw; paths are straight Cartesian segments converted to joint knots by sequential damped-least-squares IK (nullspace bias toward home, self/table collision check via mj_collision on a private MjData, multi-seed fallback, joint-jump guard) and tracked in joint space with the 0.08 rad/step limit. Grasp yaw chosen among the 4 cube-face-aligned directions by cost (deviation from forward, other cubes in the thumb zone behind the hand, path planability, joint-limit margin). Grasp site is placed at cube center (5 mm toward the fingers), closure 1.0, lift to 14 cm above the table, carry to the bin compensating the measured in-hand cube offset, lower to ~7 cm above the table, re-center using the observed cube position, two-stage release (thumb first), retreat. If the cube is not lifted or not in the bin, it retries (up to 3 attempts, before t=17 s). Known weaknesses: ~87% on practice seeds; cubes very close to the robot body (x~0.18, y~-0.12) sometimes unreachable/stuck (timeouts); occasional branch jumps in IK can swing the arm and knock cubes; last edit (shoulder-roll limit relaxed from -0.05 to 0.3 with collision check) was not re-tested.",
